gun rate in the league. Jared Goff has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Amon-Ra St. Brown, who has drawn 30% of the targets.","defense":"The Lions have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 27th or worse in all five main efficiency measures. Their one bright spot has been the pass rush, which ranks 4th in sack rate. Aidan Hutchinson has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is D.J. Wonnum, who has 5 sacks while playing only 55% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 9th highest in the league.","special":"The Lions have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 60% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 100% of field goals, which is the best in the league. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their receivers were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Jared Goff has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,485 yards. Amon-Ra St. Brown has been the clear top target with 30% of the looks and 372 receiving yards. Jahmyr Gibbs has handled most of the work in the backfield with 88% of the carries. On defense, D.J. Wonnum leads the team with 5 sacks.","coaching":"Drew Petzing is calling the offense and Kelvin Sheppard is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Vikings under Kevin O'Connell and the 2023 Browns under Kevin Stefanski. Their defense looks most like the 2022 Browns and the 2024 Bengals under Lou Anarumo.","trends":"The offense went from 7th in EPA per play in 2025 to 3rd so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 14th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 31st so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was screen rate, which went from 10% to 6%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}